Fixed bugs:
- mixing concepts of LangChain `llmType` and streaming `actionTypeId` for streaming purposes;
- selecting inline connector didn't affect immediately settings level connector select;
- override on change conversation connector `apiConfig` `provider` and `model` values when connector doesn't have it;

This PR fix most warnings. Remaining ones typically fall in the following categories:

 - public enums with private inner fields (i.e. the API exposes an opaque enum that can be built with dedicated constructors; make sense to me, I suppose we should just mute them);
 - code that is only used in tests;
 - big chunks of unused code that I don't dare remove as they seem they have/will serve a purpose.

Changes:
- updated variable usage in Bash scripts and Dockerfile;
- updated PHP and Nginx versions to 8.3 and 1.25.4 respectively;
- updated path handling and usage in Dockerfile;
- updated documentation.

In the constructor of the sidnEppContactPostalInfo class, the parameter $organisationName is set to null by default.

parent::__construct($name, $city, $countrycode, null, $street, $province, $zipcode, $type);

Because of this, when we try to get the organization of the contact Handles, we get a null value and we can't find whether the handle type is person or organization. In eppInfoContactResponse, we try to get the getContactCompanyname(), but because of the null value passing it in the constructor, always we are getting a null organisationName value.

I think it should be updated as with $organisationName instead of null.

parent::__construct($name, $city, $countrycode, $organisationName, $street, $province, $zipcode, $type);

## Introduction :pencil2:
All endpoints in dtfs-central-api should add `auditDetails` when inserting/updating data. This PR covers the update deal snapshot endpoint

## Resolution :heavy_check_mark:
- Add audit details to database changes for update deal snapshot endpoint

## Note ⚠️ 
This is a breaking change to the endpoint - the data used to be given in the form
```json
{
  "a-new-field": "data"
}
```
But now is of the form
```json
{
  "updateSnapshot": {
    "a-new-field": "data"
  },
  "user": {
    "_id": "example-id",
  }
}
```

All you need to do is:

```
client<llm> Ollama {
  provider baml-ollama-completion
  options {
    host http://localhost:11434
    model mistral
  }
}
```

